NAME
       realpath - print the full absolute path of a file

SYNOPSIS
       realpath [-e] [-m] [-s] [-q] FILE...

DESCRIPTION
       realpath prints the absolute path of each FILE, with symbolic links
       followed and . and .. removed. Only the last part may be missing
       unless -e or -m says otherwise.

OPTIONS
       -e, --canonicalize-existing
              Every part of the path must exist.

       -m, --canonicalize-missing
              No part needs to exist.

       -s, --no-symlinks
              Do not follow symbolic links; just tidy the path.

       -q, --quiet
              Do not print errors.

EXAMPLES
           realpath ../notes.txt
           realpath -s /etc/../usr/./bin

SEE ALSO
       readlink(1), pwd(1), basename(1), dirname(1)
